<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 6 January, from 1066 to 1950.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1066 CE <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Harold Godwinson crowned King of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The day after Edward the Confessor's death, Harold was crowned, probably in Westminster Abbey. William of Normandy disputed the succession and invaded that autumn, killing Harold at Hastings.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1412 CE <span class="tih-ago">614 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc is born at Domrémy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition Joan of Arc was born on Epiphany in the village of Domrémy, in north-eastern France. She led French forces to relieve Orléans in 1429, was burned in 1431 and canonised in 1920.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1838 CE <span class="tih-ago">188 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfred Vail and Samuel Morse demonstrate their telegraph</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Speedwell Ironworks in New Jersey, Vail and Morse sent messages over two miles of wire using an early form of their code. Telegraph lines soon spread across America and the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Telegraph</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1907 CE <span class="tih-ago">119 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Maria Montessori opens her first Casa dei Bambini</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a tenement in Rome's San Lorenzo district, Montessori opened a 'children's house' for working families. The child-led methods she developed there spread to schools across the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1912 CE <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfred Wegener presents his theory of continental drift</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a geology meeting in Frankfurt, Wegener argued that the continents had once formed a single landmass and drifted apart. Long rejected, the idea was vindicated by plate tectonics in the 1960s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1941 CE <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt sets out the 'Four Freedoms'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his State of the Union address, Franklin Roosevelt named freedom of speech, freedom of worship, freedom from want and freedom from fear as universal rights. The speech shaped Allied war aims and the UN.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1950 CE <span class="tih-ago">76 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain recognises the People's Republic of China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The United Kingdom became the first major Western power to recognise Mao Zedong's communist government in Beijing. The decision, partly aimed at protecting Hong Kong, split Britain from US policy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li></ol>
